(1) blocking density by denominator c  (c = e/gcd(d,e))
    c :  density   = blocked/c
     1 :  0        = 0.0000
     2 :  1/2      = 0.5000
     3 :  1/3      = 0.3333
     4 :  1/4      = 0.2500
     5 :  2/5      = 0.4000
     6 :  1/3      = 0.3333
     7 :  2/7      = 0.2857
     8 :  1/4      = 0.2500
     9 :  1/3      = 0.3333
    10 :  3/10     = 0.3000
    11 :  3/11     = 0.2727
    12 :  1/4      = 0.2500
    13 :  4/13     = 0.3077
    14 :  2/7      = 0.2857
    15 :  4/15     = 0.2667
    16 :  1/4      = 0.2500
    17 :  5/17     = 0.2941
    18 :  5/18     = 0.2778
    19 :  5/19     = 0.2632
    20 :  1/4      = 0.2500
    21 :  2/7      = 0.2857
    22 :  3/11     = 0.2727
    23 :  6/23     = 0.2609
    24 :  1/4      = 0.2500

    -> small c blocks far more than the large-c limit of 1/4.
       c = e/gcd(d,e) is small exactly when gcd(d,e) is LARGE.

(2) the budget at a flank: 6 ratios, all below 1 blocking k=0
    need sum(density) >= 1 + (m-1)/e   with m = #ratios blocking k = 0
    e=  8: six density-1/4 ratios give 1.50 vs requirement 1.625  -> SHORT
    e= 12: six density-1/4 ratios give 1.50 vs requirement 1.417  -> enough
    e= 16: six density-1/4 ratios give 1.50 vs requirement 1.312  -> enough
    e= 20: six density-1/4 ratios give 1.50 vs requirement 1.250  -> enough
    e= 30: six density-1/4 ratios give 1.50 vs requirement 1.167  -> enough

(3) what the eighth pattern actually spends (flank 8, ratios m/8):
    d=1: gcd(d,8)=1, c=8, density=1/4 = 0.2500
    d=3: gcd(d,8)=1, c=8, density=1/4 = 0.2500
    d=4: gcd(d,8)=4, c=2, density=1/2 = 0.5000
    d=5: gcd(d,8)=1, c=8, density=1/4 = 0.2500
    d=7: gcd(d,8)=1, c=8, density=1/4 = 0.2500
    total density 3/2 = 1.5000   requirement 1 + 4/8 = 1.5   -> exactly tight
